  "id": "public-health-nurse",
  "term": "public health nurse",
  "definition": "A public health nurse is a nurse who, in child health clinic visits, monitors a child’s growth and development, assesses family well-being, provides health counselling, and gives vaccinations. In this setting, the role is part of preventive health care delivered through regular scheduled check-ups.",
